cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "ALTO2TEI: an ALTO-to-TEI pipeline for early modern printed books"
abstract: >-
  A Python pipeline converting the ALTO XML produced by OCR/HTR engines into
  TEI P5 editions of early modern printed books. Layout is preserved in
  sourceDoc under the SegmOnto taxonomy with IIIF-addressable page images, the
  reading text is assembled in text, and three optional phases add linguistic
  annotation (tokens, parts of speech, lemmas), modernized spellings encoded as
  orig/reg pairs, and named entities resolved against standOff lists. Output is
  validated against a project TEI customization (ODD) that states what a
  conformant output of the pipeline is. Developed for the Projet Grand Siècle
  (Université de Lausanne, Université de Genève) on a corpus of French art
  theory and art literature printed between 1548 and 1669. The sourceDoc and
  header construction descend from earlier work by Kelly Christensen.
type: software
